    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] The Van Trump Glacier is actually a scattering of glaciers and snowfields located on the southern flank of Mount Rainier in Washington.\n[2] Stevens and Philemon Beecher Van Trump made the first documented successful climb of Mount Rainier on August 17, 1870.\n[3] Philemon Beecher Van Trump (1839–1916), also known as P. B. Van Trump, was an American pioneering mountaineer and writer who lived in the state of Washington.\n[4] She was the first woman and the first botanist to ascend Mount Kinabalu in February 1910.\n\nNotes:\n[bridge] Van Trump Glacier is named after Philemon Beecher Van Trump, who made the first documented successful climb of Mount Rainier with Hazard Stevens in 1870."
